# ARCHITECTURE GAP QUESTIONS — RELEVANT VS. IRRELEVANT

Some of the most valuable questions identify information missing from the transcript but
necessary to understand the architecture. But absence alone is never sufficient grounding — the
absence must be architecturally meaningful. Distinguish:

**Relevant architectural gap** — its absence prevents understanding an important relationship.

> "What are the inputs to the Backend API component?"

when the API is introduced but its source data is never described.

**Irrelevant theoretical gap** — could be asked of any system, but isn't necessary to understand
*this* architecture.

> "What monitoring system does the Backend API use?"

when observability is never relevant to the change being discussed.

Do not generate a question simply because some category of information is generically absent.

